  "weekLabel": "Week of Oct 19–23, 2026",
  "headline": "Quiet calendar as Anthropic's filing nears",
  "summary": "Renaissance Capital and Nasdaq show no IPOs scheduled for the week of Oct 19; only two small deals are penciled in on IPOScoop: Bitcoin-mining host Bitari (~$30M) and Hong Kong Web3 consultant Web3Labs (~$28M), both unconfirmed. All eyes are on Anthropic: IFR reports a public S-1 on Mon, Oct 26, a roadshow from Nov 9 and pricing the week after (up to ~$100B at a ~$2T valuation), while Reuters says some investors are now discussing ~$1.5T. All of that is from unnamed sources. Last week's biotechs delivered: Iambic is up 48.8% from its $16 IPO price and City Therapeutics rose 24.4% on its debut, and Retension has turned from a -12% debut to +17%. Filings were thin, just two SPACs, while Klook (~$400M est.) and BioVentrix withdrew and Nscale's IPO looks stalled by data center delays. Renaissance's IPO Index was up 12.1% YTD vs the S&P 500's 14.2% as of Oct 15.",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "text": "No IPOs on the Renaissance or Nasdaq calendars this week; IPOScoop lists two micro-caps (BIAI, MDAT)",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Anthropic's public S-1 is reported for Oct 26, with a roadshow from Nov 9 (IFR); as early as Oct 23 (Renaissance)",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "Reported, not confirmed"
    },
    {
      "text": "Iambic (IAM) +48.8% and City Therapeutics (CTY) +24.4% from their IPO prices",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Klook withdrew its ~$400M IPO; BioVentrix and SPAC Creative Future also pulled out",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Nscale's ~$35B IPO plan is reportedly muddied by data center delays",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "Reported, not confirmed"
    }
  ],
